# Purpose:
#   Single canonical registry for every external capability the federation can
#   reach. Agents never name an MCP directly — they request a canonical
#   capability (e.g. `reality.search`) and the AAA Capability Router chooses
#   the backend. One canonical name per capability. Stateless MCP servers.
#   Write tools gated by A-FORGE lease.
#
# Invariants (binding — INV-11..17, derived from F1/F4/F11/F13):
#   INV-11  one_canonical_name_per_capability          — no MCP sprawl
#   INV-12  mcp_servers_must_be_stateless              — no cognition/authority/continuity owner-ship
#   INV-13  cognition_owner   = agent                  — model + agent only
#   INV-14  authority_owner   = AAA_router             — never delegated to MCP server
#   INV-15  continuity_owner  = VAULT999 + arifFlow     — never delegated to MCP server
#   INV-16  write_tools_gated_by   = A-FORGE_lease      — F1 AMANAH
#   INV-17  credentials_held_by    = gateway_only       — F12 RESILIENCE

